html
  head
    link(rel='stylesheet' href='https://code.jquery.com/ui/1.14.1/themes/base/jquery-ui.css')
    link(rel='stylesheet', type='text/css', href='/css/styles.css')
    link(rel='preconnect' href='https://fonts.googleapis.com')
    link(rel='preconnect' href='https://fonts.gstatic.com' crossorigin)
    link(href='https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Caveat:wght@400..700&display=swap' rel='stylesheet')
    script(
      src='https://code.jquery.com/jquery-3.7.1.min.js'
      integrity='sha256-/JqT3SQfawRcv/BIHPThkBvs0OEvtFFmqPF/lYI/Cxo='
      crossorigin='anonymous'
    )
    script(
      src='https://code.jquery.com/ui/1.14.1/jquery-ui.min.js'
      integrity='sha256-AlTido85uXPlSyyaZNsjJXeCs07eSv3r43kyCVc8ChI='
      crossorigin='anonymous'
    )
    script(
      src='https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/jqueryui-touch-punch/0.2.3/jquery.ui.touch-punch.min.js'
      integrity='sha512-0bEtK0USNd96MnO4XhH8jhv3nyRF0eK87pJke6pkYf3cM0uDIhNJy9ltuzqgypoIFXw3JSuiy04tVk4AjpZdZw=='
      crossorigin='anonymous'
      referrerpolicy='no-referrer'
    )
    script(src='https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/dayjs@1/dayjs.min.js')
    script(src='https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/dayjs@1/plugin/advancedFormat.js')
    script(src='https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/dayjs@1/plugin/customParseFormat.js')
    script(src='https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/dayjs@1/plugin/weekOfYear.js')
    script.
      dayjs.extend(window.dayjs_plugin_advancedFormat)
      dayjs.extend(window.dayjs_plugin_customParseFormat)
      dayjs.extend(window.dayjs_plugin_weekOfYear)
    script(type='module' src='/js/modules/cs-sheet.js')
    script(src='/js/cs-sheet.js')
    title='Customer & Sales Totals'
  body
    dialog(id='whatIsThis')
      div(class='header-with-button')
        h1='Office Folk Art'
        button(command='close' commandfor='whatIsThis')
          h3='Close'
      p
        | Since the evolution of advanced cognition and aesthetic sensibility in humans, we as a
        | species have had the insatiable desire to <strong>create</strong>. Regardless of race,
        | sex, gender, religion, culture, nationality, or archaeological period, the desire to
        | express oneself is hard-coded in our genome, and one way or another, we will each find
        | ways to give our innermost thoughts, feelings, fears, and desires a tangible form. What
        | form this takes, exactly, is up to the discretion of its creator; often times, one is
        | limited by one's immediate environment and the tools available therein. One recalls the
        | plight of the venerable Marquis de Sade, whose imprisonment in 1785 forced the genially
        | perverse writer to pen his magnum opus <em>Les 120 Journées de Sodome</em> on small
        | pieces of contraband paper painstakingly glued together.
      p
        | During the mid-1990s through the late 2000s, the rapid adoption of computer technology
        | in workplaces both large and small, white-collar and blue-collar, by the lowliest
        | unpaid-intern-personal-assistant to the well-heeled President of Engineering they serve,
        | for email-drafting, spreadsheet-designing, project management, and every other
        | conceivable task ripe for automation or expedition by digital electronics meant that it
        | only be a matter of time before the anonymous mouse-clicking, keyboard-tapping office
        | worker would discover the surprising versatility of the office workstation as a tool for
        | creative expression. This was a time before social media; a time before the Amazon and
        | Facebook oligarchs set both precedent and a detailed template for re-programming peoples'
        | attention spans, atrophying their biological urge to create, and ultimately
        | indoctrinating them into the non-denominational Church of Passive Consumption. This was
        | a time of boredom; a time when one had to rely on one's own wit, intuition, and shrewd
        | resourcefulness to lighten the hands on the clock above their desk <em>just enough</em>
        | to accelerate the passage of time.
      p
        | This page contains an interactive tactile art exhibit wherein 105 digital graphics
        | created by an anonymous retail front-end manager between February 2002 and April 2004.
        | Each graphic was incorporated onto the lower-right (or, in one case, upper-right) corner
        | of an 8.5"x11" sheet of paper, upon which weekly customer and sales volume data were
        | hand-written into a series of Microsoft Excel tables and stored in a binder for posterity.
      p(class='gallery w4')
        a(href='/img/cs-sheet/example/cs1.jpg' target='_blank')
          img(src='/img/cs-sheet/example/cs1.jpg')
        a(href='/img/cs-sheet/example/cs2.jpg' target='_blank')
          img(src='/img/cs-sheet/example/cs2.jpg')
        a(href='/img/cs-sheet/example/cs3.jpg' target='_blank')
          img(src='/img/cs-sheet/example/cs3.jpg')
        a(href='/img/cs-sheet/example/cs4.jpg' target='_blank')
          img(src='/img/cs-sheet/example/cs4.jpg')
      p
        | We know not their name nor their motive. We know not the specifics of their brush, nor
        | their canvas, nor their palette. Yet we know with near-laser-precision exactly what they
        | were thinking and what they were feeling on any given date, within a four-day margin of
        | error - in historian terms, a near-bullseye that allows us to piece together a narrative
        | of an ordinary human being, spanning over two years of their professional life. In this
        | curated collection of digital word art - painstakingly captured and restored for optimal
        | viewing through a World Wide Web browser window - we not only see our friends, neighbors,
        | and colleagues, but also ourselves.
    include includes/header.pug
    div(class='cs-container')
      div(class='cs-days')
        div(class='cs-day-sunday')
          day-block(data-day-of-week="Sunday")
        div(class='cs-day-monday')
          day-block(data-day-of-week="Monday")
        div(class='cs-day-tuesday')
          day-block(data-day-of-week="Tuesday")
        div(class='cs-day-wednesday')
          day-block(data-day-of-week="Wednesday")
        div(class='cs-vertical-decal')
          div(id='verticalDecal')
        div(class='cs-day-thursday' style='grid-area: b1')
          day-block(data-day-of-week="Thursday")
        div(class='cs-day-friday' style='grid-area: b2')
          day-block(data-day-of-week="Friday")
        div(class='cs-day-saturday' style='grid-area: b3')
          day-block(data-day-of-week="Saturday")
        div(class='cs-day-decal' style='grid-area: b4')
          div(id='cornerDecal' style='width: 400px')
      div(class='cs-toolbox')
        button(command='show-modal' commandfor='whatIsThis')
          h2='What is this?'
        p='On the left, you will find a replica of a C&S sheet, almost identical to its real-life equivalent.'
        p='On the right (this side), you will find various settings to alter the appearance of the C&S sheet.'
        p='All settings and their possible values were extracted via thorough analysis of 105 different C&S sheets.'
        div(class='cs-toolbox-hints')
          div(id='toolbox' class='ui-widget-toolkit')
            h3(class='ui-widget-header')='Options'
            div(class='input-group')
              label(for='week')='Week of:'
              input(type='week' name='week' id='week')
            div(class='input-group')
              label(for='decal')='Decal:'
              select(name='decal' id='decal')
                option(value='')='--'
                each decal in decals
                  option(value=decal)=decal
            div(class='input-group')
              label(for='tableStyle')='Table color scheme:'
              select(name='tableStyle' id='tableStyle')
                option(value='bw')='Black & White'
                option(value='classic1' selected)='Classic 1'
                option(value='classic2')='Classic 2'
                option(value='classic3')='Classic 3'
            div(class='input-group vertical')
              div='Decal placement:'
              div
                input(type='radio', name='decalPlacement', id='decalBottomRight', value='1', checked)
                label(for='decalBottomRight')='Bottom-right corner'
              div
                input(type='radio', name='decalPlacement', id='decalTopRight', value='2')
                label(for='decalTopRight')='Top-right corner'
            div(class='input-group')
              label(for='dateFormat')='Date format:'
              select(name='dateFormat' id='dateFormat')
                option(value='D-MMM-YY')='D-MMM-YY'
                option(value='M/DD.YY')='M/DD.YY'
                option(value='M\\DD\\.YY')='M\\DD\\.YY'
                option(value='M\\DD\\YY')='M\\DD\\YY'
                option(value='M\\DDYY')='M\\DDYY'
                option(value='M/DD/YYYY')='M/DD/YYYY'
                option(value='MDD/YYYY')='MDD/YYYY'
                option(value='M/D/YY' selected)='M/D/YY'
                option(value='M/D//YYYY')='M/D//YYYY'
                option(value='M/D/YYYY')='M/D/YYYY'
                option(value='M/DYYYY')='M/DYYYY'
                option(value='MMM D')='MMM D'
                option(value='MMM DD/YY')='MMM DD/YY'
                option(value='MMM/D.YY')='MMM/D.YY'
                option(value='MMMM DD\\YY')='MMMM DD\\YY'
                option(value='MMMM D,YYYY')='MMMM D,YYYY'
                option(value='#######')='#######'
            div(class='input-group vertical')
              div
                input(type='checkbox', id='uppercaseHeader', name='headerEffects', value='true')
                label(for='uppercaseHeader')='Uppercase day of week'
              div
                input(type='checkbox', id='boldHeader', name='headerEffects', value='true', checked)
                label(for='boldHeader')='Bold day of week'
              div
                input(type='checkbox', id='grayscale',  name='grayscale', value='true')
                label(for='grayscale')='Grayscale'
            div(class='input-group')
              input(type='range', id='dateOffset', name='dateOffset', min="0", max="25", step="1", value="0")
              label(for='dateOffset')='Date offset'
            button(onclick='window.print()')='🖨️ Print!'
          div
            span='Tips:'
            ul
              li='Decals are draggable and can be moved and resized.'
              li='Text can be entered into each cell.'
              li='Only black and white printing is available :( we don\'t have any budget for toner'
            p='Libraries used to make this:'
            ul
              li!='<a href="https://jquery.com/" target="_blank">jQuery</a>'
              li!='<a href="https://jqueryui.com/" target="_blank">jQuery UI</a>, for <code>.draggable()</code> and <code>.resizable()</code> extensions'
              li!='<a href="https://github.com/furf/jquery-ui-touch-punch" target=_"blank">jQuery UI Touch Punch</a>, so jQuery UI dragging and resizing can work on mobile'
              li!='<a href="https://lit.dev/" target="_blank">lit.js</a>, for custom day-table <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Web_components" target="_blank">Web Component</a>'
              li!='<a href="https://day.js.org/" target="_blank">day.js</a>, with <code>advancedFormat</code>, <code>customParseFormat</code>, and <code>weekOfYear</code> extensions, for parsing week picker'